sparky-stereo-partners (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * llama.cpp, the other local engine (Daniel's answer: "Ollama, with
    llama.cpp as the fallback", a path the person chooses): an interface of
    its own, llama.cpp on this computer, and its row on the page: install
    (Debian's llama-server with ggml's Vulkan back end, the size shown first,
    through the same pkexec helper), turn on and off, its models (the files
    in ~/.local/share/llama.cpp/models; it downloads no model by itself),
    "Open the models folder" and "Look again". Its user service,
    sparky-stereo-llama-server.service, is installed off; it starts
    llama-server in router mode on 127.0.0.1:8080, offline, on the card the
    Partners choice names, and lets only this computer's own pages call it
    from a browser (--cors-origins localhost). Debian's llama.cpp-services is
    not installed: its system service would start at installation.
  * Ollama's service: "Sign in…" through the local engine (Ollama's own
    route: ollama.com's page opens in the browser, and Ollama's key for this
    computer is linked to the account there), "Check", "Sign out", and
    whether this computer is signed in, said with what signing in sends
    (the computer's name and Ollama's key, kept by Ollama in
    ~/.ollama/id_ed25519). Commands: account, signin, signout (exit status
    7: not signed in, the address printed).
  * The page: the Card, Interface and Model lists take the width their
    longest entry needs (or the page's); a provider's name and address end
    before its Remove button, elided with the whole text in a tooltip; each
    engine's name stands at the top of its block, on the line of its state.
  * The card's Now: line says when Automatic chose the processor because no
    card has the memory of its own for the proposed model, or left such a
    card out (sparky-stereo-graphics 0.2.17's reasons).
  * KDE's text add-ons: KMail's choice also answers Kontact and the Sieve
    editor (ProgramInfo Also=), resolve prints the interface's protocol
    (PARTNER_KIND), and the KMail row says that the add-ons can follow only
    Ollama for now (their llama.cpp add-on is unfinished in 2.1.2, and they
    know no provider's own address).
  * Sixteen new sentences in English and pt_BR.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

sparky-stereo-partners (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release (ORDER 70): the Partners page of System Settings, a
    category of its own at the top, with the system defaults for text,
    speech, image and 3D (interface, model, card), the local engine (install
    with the runner the hardware setup names, on and off, models with their
    sizes, downloads held on a metered connection), providers with their
    keys in KDE Wallet, and each program's own choice; its command
    sparky-stereo-partners; the system defaults in
    /etc/xdg/sparky-stereo-partnersrc.

